      "trend": "The trend in the research on high-entropy alloys (HEAs) is focused on developing new processing methods, such as selective laser melting (SLM) and laser powder bed fusion (LPBF), to improve their microstructure, mechanical properties, and high-temperature performance. Researchers are also exploring the effects of varying alloy compositions, such as the addition of Cr, on the properties of HEAs. Furthermore, there is a growing interest in using computational methods, such as high-throughput screening, to discover new HEAs with optimized properties.",
